  "about": "Exercise names to lifts, shared word for word with the iPhone app (Track-iOS Core/Sources/TrackCore/Resources/lifts.json). A name is normalised (see lib/lift-detection.ts), its phrases and words swapped for standard ones, then the first lift whose match fits wins, so specific movements sit above generic ones. at: estimated one-rep max as a multiple of bodyweight for Novice, Solid, Strong and Elite (a rough guide, between common male and female standards); no at = recognised but never ranked. perSide: the standard is one side's weight. pair: with a dumbbell in each hand, their total counts this many times against the barbell standard. bodyweight: the share of bodyweight moved, plus any added weight (or minus assistance). also: more parts whose rank groups it counts toward, for full-body lifts. machine: only exists on a machine or cable. gear: only when the name says that equipment. parts: each muscle and the rank group it counts toward, in order (Core has none). standards: each group's main lift; an exercise moved to a group is measured on it when its own lift has no standard.",
